1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,566
Welcome back

2
00:00:01,566 --> 00:00:05,066
Today we are going to play a new pack called The Winter Rescue

3
00:00:05,633 --> 00:00:10,166
Once again we find ourselves in a custom spawn which looks like a crushed shuttle

4
00:00:10,633 --> 00:00:15,600
And, before we even open the quest book for some lore, the lore found us

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:20,800
And this time it is not just a wall of text but a whole sequence of images

6
00:00:21,466 --> 00:00:25,633
We could skip this, but I think it looks cool and it deserves to be shown

7
00:00:25,633 --> 00:00:28,500
so slow down the video if you want more immersion

8
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,333
And finally we survived

9
00:00:31,333 --> 00:00:35,833
I mean, not only from the rocket crush but also from the long introduction

10
00:00:36,766 --> 00:00:38,933
And now our adventure shall begin

11
00:00:39,466 --> 00:00:44,500
After finding a way out of that wrecked ship, we start collecting the basic materials

12
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:50,833
The first thing we look for is gravel, which is found underneath the Oxide Daisy flower

13
00:00:51,733 --> 00:00:54,300
Then we gather some sticks from some bushes

14
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:57,100
And with the help of a rudimentary flint knife

15
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:00,900
we can also take some vines out of those leaves

16
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:05,066
But, to do anything more complex, we will need a crafting table

17
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:08,833
And this one works within world item placement

18
00:01:08,833 --> 00:01:13,466
So, we fill in the grid and then we complete the crafting with a process knife

19
00:01:13,466 --> 00:01:20,400
And the first thing we craft is a drying rack, so that we can get some straw from the vines we collected earlier on

20
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:25,300
With that, we can make some rope, which we can use to craft our first tools

21
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:30,533
Now that we have a pickaxe, we can spend the rest of the night collecting stone

22
00:01:30,533 --> 00:01:33,866
which, as expected, comes in different variants

23
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:37,500
And after a long night, finally day is coming

24
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:45,333
Since the weather forecast is good, we can go outside and plow some snow, collect some wood and a bunch of other materials

25
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:48,633
Since we are getting cold and it's getting dark again

26
00:01:48,633 --> 00:01:51,333
we craft a campfire for our next night

27
00:01:51,533 --> 00:01:55,100
We throw some fuel inside it and then pitch it on fire

28
00:01:55,466 --> 00:02:00,333
This can also be used to light some sticks on fire, making torches

29
00:02:00,333 --> 00:02:03,666
But this is not the only thing we can do with fire

30
00:02:03,666 --> 00:02:05,700
We can also make pottery clens

31
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,466
and the first one shall be used to smooth some stone

32
00:02:09,466 --> 00:02:16,966
The first usage we have for stone is a tree stump, which we can use to chop down tree lumbers into planks

33
00:02:16,966 --> 00:02:19,100
Or to hammer stone into slabs

34
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:23,100
With those we can finally make our first chest

35
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:27,333
Which, as you can tell by our inability to pick it up, was really needed

36
00:02:27,333 --> 00:02:32,733
After cleaning our inventory, we smash some flux out of some sedimentary stone

37
00:02:32,733 --> 00:02:35,866
Next, we fire that up to get some quicklime

38
00:02:36,533 --> 00:02:41,033
Meanwhile, we prepare some clay buckets and fire those into ceramic buckets

39
00:02:41,433 --> 00:02:45,766
Now we can fill a barrel with water and dissolve some quicklime in it

40
00:02:46,033 --> 00:02:48,766
Finally, we add some sand to make mortar

41
00:02:48,766 --> 00:02:51,266
And it was then that a storm caught us unprepared

42
00:02:51,433 --> 00:02:57,833
If we go outside, we can barely see anything, and the temperature reached minus 60 degrees

43
00:02:58,533 --> 00:03:02,866
Before freezing to death, we go back to our campfire to warm up

44
00:03:02,866 --> 00:03:09,333
And then we go back to processing some bricks, which will be part of our future bloomery

45
00:03:09,333 --> 00:03:13,833
For that, we are also going to need some copper and some treated wood

46
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:20,733
Looking for new resources right now is an issue since there is a storm ongoing, so we work with what we have

47
00:03:20,733 --> 00:03:26,100
Luckily we have enough materials to get a creosote funnel and some piles of logs to char

48
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:33,100
We place the funnel on the bottom of a pile of logs, and then we ignite the thing as if we were on terra firma

49
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:38,800
After waiting not too much time, the process is complete and we can gather some charcoal

50
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:44,066
But, what we were looking for at the moment was the leftover creosote oil

51
00:03:44,066 --> 00:03:46,800
Which we use to seal some wood planks

52
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,000
Those are used to craft bellows

53
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,700
but it looks like we also need some leather for that

54
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:54,766
Luckily the storm is now gone

55
00:03:54,966 --> 00:03:57,966
so we can go outside and hunt some walking leather

56
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:00,633
But that's not ready yet

57
00:04:00,633 --> 00:04:03,600
We have to first clean it up from all of the fur it had

58
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:08,400
Now that we have our bellows, we only need a couple of copper ingots

59
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:13,400
Since the weather is now good, we can go outside and look for some copper

60
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:16,000
Which luckily wasn't too hard to find

61
00:04:16,366 --> 00:04:19,100
The issue is turning that into a sheet

62
00:04:20,266 --> 00:04:23,333
We start by panning the raw malachite ore out of the gravel

63
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:27,033
We put that in a clay jar with some charcoal

64
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:31,866
After firing it up, we can break the jar to retrieve our copper

65
00:04:32,166 --> 00:04:37,133
To make a plate we just put our cold ingots on a wood anvil and smash with our hammer

66
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:39,733
No need for tedious minigames

67
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:42,666
With that, we can now craft our tuyere

68
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:48,200
However, it looks like there's something else we have to do before we can get our bloomery

69
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:53,900
The first thing is a research station so we can unlock the crafting recipe of the machine

70
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:59,266
But, even if we did that, we would have no materials to work inside it

71
00:04:59,266 --> 00:05:02,100
So, instead of researching the bloomery

72
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:07,200
our first research shall be some tools that will help us find some raw minerals to work

73
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:10,433
And, after committing some stone to that research

74
00:05:10,433 --> 00:05:13,333
we find the missing clues in a copper ingot

75
00:05:13,333 --> 00:05:17,100
Now we have the required knowledge to craft a prospector pick

76
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:20,266
And the first thing we found is lignite

77
00:05:20,266 --> 00:05:26,100
Usually that's the most useless kind of fuel, but here it can be converted into coal

78
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:29,466
But that's still not the mineral we need for our progression

79
00:05:30,033 --> 00:05:35,900
So, to have an easier time finding some iron, we research even better prospecting tools

80
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:39,633
But this time, we also have to do some paperwork

81
00:05:40,266 --> 00:05:42,366
Since we don't have access to paper yet

82
00:05:42,533 --> 00:05:46,733
we shall use a stone plate and some charcoals to draw our schemes

83
00:05:46,966 --> 00:05:50,466
And now we have a new research minigame to figure out

84
00:05:51,033 --> 00:05:55,233
And it looks like we just have to pick matching pairs of items

85
00:05:55,233 --> 00:06:01,333
So, after quickly doing all the paperwork, we need one more clue, a prospector pick

86
00:06:01,333 --> 00:06:06,633
With that, we now have our prospector core spade, which will be way more helpful

87
00:06:06,633 --> 00:06:12,200
And, after some more exploration and prospecting, we found some iron-rich minerals

88
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:19,133
But, before reaching iron, we gather some tin and some more copper to make some bronze for a better pickaxe

89
00:06:19,133 --> 00:06:25,200
With that, we gather some magnetite which was also required to start the bloomery research

90
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:27,600
We quickly do the research minigame

91
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:30,033
And examine some stuff

92
00:06:30,966 --> 00:06:34,500
Thus finishing the research which allows us to build our bloomery

93
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:39,333
Once the structure is in place, we fill it with magnetite and charcoal

94
00:06:39,833 --> 00:06:42,466
then we pitch it on fire and blow air on it

95
00:06:42,466 --> 00:06:47,100
Once the process is completed and the fire is out, we gather our iron

96
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:54,200
With that we can now move on to the steam age, where we can finally unlock a normal crafting table

97
00:06:54,200 --> 00:07:01,533
And our rewards is more chunk claims, which remind us that we should stop for a moment to build a proper base

98
00:07:01,533 --> 00:07:07,633
But, before that, we shall get some more quality of life, such as snowshoes

99
00:07:07,633 --> 00:07:11,533
And we must not forget to add some insulating straw to our clothing

100
00:07:12,033 --> 00:07:17,200
With our new shoes, we can run to our new shelter, made out of packed snow

101
00:07:17,566 --> 00:07:24,033
Here we can have a nice room with all of our stuff and also an alloy kiln, which will make melting stuff easier

102
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:29,033
This is nice and all, but we should also worry about food

103
00:07:29,033 --> 00:07:34,700
The rations we savaged from our ships are running out, so we need something to put in our new pot

104
00:07:35,566 --> 00:07:41,266
During our expedition, we found some frozen stuff which we can defrost on our campfire

105
00:07:41,666 --> 00:07:45,433
And, with that, we now have some seeds to plant

106
00:07:45,433 --> 00:07:49,233
But not all of those plants can grow in this climate

107
00:07:49,233 --> 00:07:53,733
But some do, so we shall have a diet based on rye and turnips

108
00:07:54,266 --> 00:08:01,066
And we can integrate with some extra stuff, such as mushrooms, which we can grow on our armor with our body heat

109
00:08:01,333 --> 00:08:04,700
With all of that stuff we can make a nice stew

110
00:08:04,933 --> 00:08:07,666
But we will also need something to drink

111
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:11,766
And the water in this place is all dirty and cold

112
00:08:11,766 --> 00:08:13,166
So we boil it

113
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:16,700
But that was not a balanced enough diet

114
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:20,300
And since we are all so mentally exhausted and out of inspiration

115
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:25,100
we take an opportunity on this sunny day to go and do some outside activities

116
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:28,466
such as placing a campfire on an iced lake

117
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:32,000
We take off our clothes and then we take a nice refreshing bath

118
00:08:32,433 --> 00:08:40,566
And here we also found a source of proteins, some kelps, and also some ruins of an ancient civilization

119
00:08:41,533 --> 00:08:47,100
But we can't keep the breath for long enough to explore those ruins and we are also getting cold

120
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:52,466
So, we dry out the campfire, put on our dress and go back to the millstone

121
00:08:52,966 --> 00:08:59,066
And looking at that thing spin gave us some inspiration for something even more spinny, a mixer

122
00:08:59,066 --> 00:09:04,100
And with that we can mix up some fire clay, which we can use for a blast furnace

123
00:09:04,166 --> 00:09:08,666
But there is something else that moves up and down, a forge hammer

124
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:12,600
This will allow us to convert 3 ingots to 2 plates

125
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:16,433
giving us the first upgrade from hammering ingots on our wood anvil

126
00:09:16,866 --> 00:09:20,533
However, working that thing by hand is quite hard and slow

127
00:09:20,933 --> 00:09:25,466
So we start working on a way to not have to manually crank those heavy machinery

128
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:29,933
But it looks like we can't fit those schematics in our stone tablets

129
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,700
So we start working on something to help us with our research

130
00:09:34,266 --> 00:09:38,700
And after a lot of more manual work, we manage to get some proper paper

131
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:40,633
Then we get some ink

132
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:46,766
And, with those new tools, we can finally get into researching more complex stuff

133
00:09:47,533 --> 00:09:53,533
And, after an intensive studying session, we manage to fully understand how steam engines work

134
00:09:53,533 --> 00:09:57,800
We studied so intensively that we also crafted one in the meantime

135
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:02,800
And since crafting more is going to be problematic, we have to use it properly

136
00:10:03,266 --> 00:10:06,366
We start by laying down a burning box with a boiler

137
00:10:06,733 --> 00:10:10,766
Then we add a pump and manually crank it to fill the boiler with water

138
00:10:11,333 --> 00:10:14,000
Finally, we add the engine with its flywheel

139
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:17,933
Now we just add some fuel and our machine will start working

140
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,900
And to increase its strength we can add a pump

141
00:10:21,333 --> 00:10:24,100
Which, of course, can be pushed by the engine

142
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:27,833
And we can watch our forge hammer work faster

143
00:10:28,033 --> 00:10:33,833
But what we really need that power for is crafting bigger things, such as a mechanical calculator

144
00:10:34,266 --> 00:10:36,700
And that is one quite heavy machine

145
00:10:37,433 --> 00:10:39,900
And from that machine we get research points

146
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:43,600
which are now starting to become required to complete our research

147
00:10:43,933 --> 00:10:46,666
And with those points we now unlock ore doubling

148
00:10:47,633 --> 00:10:51,666
But this room is crammed and we are already rebuilding stuff too often

149
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:55,433
So we made a new room where we can keep all of our machinery

150
00:10:55,466 --> 00:11:02,233
To use them, we fuel our boiler, then we manually crank the pumps until the engine starts spinning

151
00:11:02,766 --> 00:11:07,866
Once it gets some traction, we engage the gears that will connect the pumps to the engine

152
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:11,866
And now we have leftover power to turn on our workshop machinery

153
00:11:12,133 --> 00:11:16,600
And the machines are now going to work way faster than we were manually cranking

154
00:11:16,866 --> 00:11:19,933
And work more efficiently with the better gear ratios

155
00:11:20,833 --> 00:11:22,866
But making that workshop was not easy

156
00:11:23,333 --> 00:11:24,800
We run into many difficulties

157
00:11:24,833 --> 00:11:28,500
Starting from the diseases caused by our poor diet

158
00:11:28,733 --> 00:11:36,933
So we made an incubator where we start cultivating bacteria to make weird stuff that resemble chocolate that we can integrate in our diet

159
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:39,600
But that's not the only thing we made

160
00:11:39,766 --> 00:11:45,633
We also set up some fish traps to get some real proteins and also some plant oil

161
00:11:45,733 --> 00:11:49,600
And to keep warm underwater we can use this handy hand stove

162
00:11:50,366 --> 00:11:52,733
And to finish our quality of life improvements

163
00:11:52,766 --> 00:11:56,966
We also have a new water filter where we can refill our new thermos

164
00:11:57,233 --> 00:11:59,666
But, to truly fix our issues

165
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:03,466
We will need to start cultivating a higher variety of plants

166
00:12:03,900 --> 00:12:06,600
The main issue is that they won't grow on snow

167
00:12:06,933 --> 00:12:10,433
And the dirt bellow is too icy to grow those crops

168
00:12:10,866 --> 00:12:13,833
So, to warm up the ground in a large area

169
00:12:13,866 --> 00:12:18,366
We retrieved the core of our ship and used it to build a large heat generator

170
00:12:18,733 --> 00:12:21,466
And while this will make the soil more fertile

171
00:12:21,533 --> 00:12:23,933
It will also burn a lot of fuel

172
00:12:24,833 --> 00:12:27,600
But what matters is that we can now grow wheat

173
00:12:28,133 --> 00:12:31,333
Once we have some, we can crush it into flour

174
00:12:31,533 --> 00:12:33,466
That we can use for make dough

175
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:35,400
But eating that is not healthy

176
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:38,800
So we add some lime dye to make slime balls

177
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:41,533
And with those we can make some glue

178
00:12:41,833 --> 00:12:45,133
Which means that we can now make contraptions

179
00:12:45,433 --> 00:12:48,233
And thus we have automated the fuel production

180
00:12:49,133 --> 00:12:51,633
You probably notice how slow it's working

181
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:56,766
And that's because we wanted to keep some of our power producing for the rest of the workshop

182
00:12:56,766 --> 00:13:02,566
But that was still not enough, so we doubled our capacity by moving to the cast iron tier

183
00:13:02,566 --> 00:13:06,300
And most of that power is going inside our new dynamo

184
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:08,833
which will produce some electricity

185
00:13:09,266 --> 00:13:12,433
which we can use to finally obtain some steel

186
00:13:12,433 --> 00:13:18,766
And to make the process go smoother, we shall use our new assembly line to make our first capacitor

187
00:13:18,766 --> 00:13:22,800
For the next task we are going back in our greening garden

188
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:26,133
where we tap some latex from a (?) tree

189
00:13:26,133 --> 00:13:29,800
We mix that with some sulfur to make vulcanized rubber

190
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:33,633
which we can use to finally unlock mechanical belts

191
00:13:33,633 --> 00:13:38,900
Finally, to complete the steam age tier, we quickly craft our first circuitry

192
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:43,466
and we shall use our first circuit for a simple electrolyzer

193
00:13:43,466 --> 00:13:50,700
which of course is going to electrolyze water, or more precisely salt water to get sodium hydroxide

194
00:13:50,700 --> 00:13:54,233
and I guess the leftover gases are vented

195
00:13:54,233 --> 00:14:02,400
Anyways, we wash up some bauxite and then we mix it with sodium hydroxide to extract aluminium hydroxide

196
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:06,600
We blast it with lava heat to get aluminium oxide

197
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:11,500
But to extract aluminium from that we are going to need some cryolite

198
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:15,133
which is going to be just a few more chemical steps

199
00:14:15,133 --> 00:14:20,200
After quickly doing those things, we are ready to cook our first aluminium ingot

200
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:23,966
And getting there was a GrogTech tier-worthy experience

201
00:14:23,966 --> 00:14:28,433
Now that we are on fire, we do not want to go back to RF machinery

202
00:14:28,433 --> 00:14:30,933
so we look into a more complex heat generator

203
00:14:30,933 --> 00:14:36,333
Since to complete our research in conventional ways we would need too many expensive blocks

204
00:14:36,333 --> 00:14:41,533
we instead opt for fueling our research with expensive but easy-to-find coal

205
00:14:41,533 --> 00:14:44,233
And there we have our tier-2 generator

206
00:14:44,233 --> 00:14:47,100
The upgrade consists in a tank for fluids

207
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:52,666
We can add steam to increase the range and heating our water to power a heat pipe

208
00:14:52,666 --> 00:14:58,766
And the first thing we shall do with that extra heat is feed a steam charger to fill our new heater vest

209
00:14:58,766 --> 00:15:02,433
With that thing equipped, not even a blizzard can stop us

210
00:15:02,433 --> 00:15:08,133
And after fooling around the whole night with our hot drinks, a hot sauna is what we need

211
00:15:08,133 --> 00:15:12,133
That gave us a lot of inspiration, so much that we realized that

212
00:15:12,133 --> 00:15:17,433
instead of wasting steam like that, we can instead feed it to a compact steam engine

213
00:15:17,433 --> 00:15:23,100
which we can use to self-power our farm and have even more leftover fuel for our workshop

214
00:15:23,100 --> 00:15:28,400
which is now equipped with a bending machine that can make plates, rods and wires

215
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:32,600
And now we can make a big enough batch of circuits and motors

216
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:37,333
We have motors. We have circuits. We have servo cores

217
00:15:37,333 --> 00:15:41,133
Which means we can now unlock many new machines

218
00:15:41,133 --> 00:15:46,733
However, with those upgrades, our factory has now hit the current end of our adventure

219
00:15:46,733 --> 00:15:52,400
But fear not, we will come back when the new materials and generators will be released

220
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:53,000
Bye bye

